<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Re, Crawford complete venture.</title>
<headline>Swiss Re, Crawford complete venture.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Reinsurance Co said it and Crawford &amp; Co of Atlanta had completed their agreement to merge Crawford's non-U.S. claims services business with similar units of the Thomas Howell Group.</p>
<p>The new company, Crawford-THG Ltd, will specialise in the area of loss adjustment and claims management.</p>
<p>Crawford will own 60 percent of the venture and Swiss Re the remaining 40 percent, Swiss Re said in a statement.</p>
<p>The venture should have annual sales of some $200 million and offices in some 50 countries.</p>
<p>Its unit in the United Kingdom will be the largest independent adjusting firm in that market with more than $90 million in annual revenues.</p>
<p>--  Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
